{"id":"chatcmpl-726aff8a44b9436a9cf365fa494beff2","object":"chat.completion","created":1790609588,"model":"accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"Let me analyze this task. I need to extract reported financial-statement facts from the supplied official filing documents (a Form 20-F for Grupo Aeroméxico, ticker AERO).\n\nThe requested fields are:\n1. AssetsCurrent - Total current assets on consolidated balance sheet as of 2025-12-31\n2. Assets - Total assets on consolidated balance sheet as of 2025-12-31\n3. LiabilitiesCurrent - Total current liabilities on consolidated balance sheet as of 2025-12-31\n4. Liabilities - Total liabilities on consolidated balance sheet as of 2025-12-31\n5. Equity - Total equity on consolidated balance sheet as of 2025-12-31\n6. EquityAndLiabilities - Total equity and liabilities on consolidated balance sheet as of 2025-12-31\n7. NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities - Net cash from operating activities for 2025-01-01 to 2025-12-31\n\nLet me look at the document carefully.\n\nFirst, there's the \"Consolidated Statements of Financial Position Data\" table (T:A:385) in Item 5 (Operating Results section) which is a summary table in millions of U.S. dollars. This is a summary table derived from audited statements, not the primary financial statement itself. Per the instructions: \"Do not use a note, segment table, summary, non-GAAP table, or parent-only statement when the requested definition requires a consolidated primary-statement value.\"\n\nSo I should use the actual primary financial statements: \"Consolidated statements of financial position\" which appears at T:A:638 (assets) and T:A:639 (liabilities and equity). These are in thousands of US dollars.\n\nFrom T:A:638 (Consolidated statements of financial position):\n- \"Total current assets\" row (S:A:C638.12.1): 2025 value = 1,979,596 (thousands USD), tagged as ifrs-full:CurrentAssets;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3\n- \"Total assets\" row (S:A:C638.24.1): 2025 value = 7,193,091 (thousands USD), tagged as ifrs-full:Assets;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025\n\nFrom T:A:639 (Consolidated statements of financial position (continued)):\n- \"Total current liabilities\" row (S:A:C639.13.1): 2025 value = 3,095,938 (thousands USD), tagged as ifrs-full:CurrentLiabilities;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025\n- \"Total liabilities\" row (S:A:C639.24.1): 2025 value = 7,785,307 (thousands USD), tagged as ifrs-full:Liabilities;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025\n- \"Total equity (deficit)\" row (S:A:C639.39.1): 2025 value = (592,216), tagged as ifrs-full:Equity;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025 with sgn=- (negative)\n- \"Total equity (deficit) and liabilities\" row (S:A:C639.41.1): 2025 value = 7,193,091, tagged as ifrs-full:EquityAndLiabilities;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025\n\nFrom T:A:645 (Consolidated statements of cash flows):\n- \"Net cash from operating activities\" row (S:A:C645.36.1): 2025 value = 913,081 (thousands USD), tagged as ifrs-full:CashFlowsFromUsedInOperatingActivities;ctx=P01_01_2025To12_31_2025\n\nNow, about the scale: The statement header says \"(In thousands of US dollars)\". The XBRL tags have u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3, which means scale 3 (thousands). So the scale is \"3\" — wait, the schema says scale pattern \"^[1-9][0-9]*$\", so scale should be recorded as a string like \"3\" for thousands, \"6\" for millions, etc.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me think about what \"scale\" means here. The instruction says: \"Record the statement's scale separately; do not multiply it.\" So if the statement is \"In thousands of US dollars\", the scale is 1000 (10^3). The scale field pattern allows \"^[1-9][0-9]*$\" — positive integers. So scale could be \"1000\" (i.e., 10^3) or \"3\" (the exponent). Hmm.\n\nThe schema says scale is a string matching ^[1-9][0-9]*$. This means it must start with a nonzero digit and be composed of digits. Both \"3\" and \"1000\" match. Which one is intended? The typical convention in these extraction tasks: scale = the multiplier as a power-of-ten exponent or the actual multiplier? Let me think.\n\n\"Record the statement's scale separately; do not multiply it.\" The statement scale is \"in thousands\" = 1,000. So scale = \"1000\" seems most literal. But some conventions use \"3\" for thousands. Hmm.\n\nGiven the pattern ^[1-9][0-9]*$ matches both \"3\" and \"1000\", I'll go with \"1000\" as the actual scale multiplier since the statement says \"In thousands of US dollars\". Actually, let me reconsider — in many similar extraction schemas, scale is expressed as the power of 10 multiplier, e.g., \"1000\" for thousands, \"1000000\" for millions. That seems most defensible. I'll use \"1000\".\n\nHmm, but wait. Actually let me reconsider. Some schemas use scale as the exponent (e.g., \"3\" means thousands). The instruction \"Record the statement's scale separately\" suggests recording the scale as stated in the document. The document states \"(In thousands of US dollars)\". The scale multiplier is 1,000. I'll use \"1000\".\n\nNow, for the summary table in Item 5 (T:A:385), values are in millions of U.S. dollars. But the instruction says not to use summary tables. However, I should cite checked locations. For \"found\" results, I need one location (the location field). But I could also cross-check. The schema for found has only \"location\" (single). The ambiguous/not_found have checked_locations (min 2 for ambiguous, min 1 for not_found).\n\nHmm, but wait — should I be careful about whether the primary statement is indeed the consolidated primary statement? Yes. The \"Consolidated statements of financial position\" (T:A:638, T:A:639) are the primary balance sheets. The \"Consolidated statements of cash flows\" (T:A:645) is the primary cash flow statement. These are in the audited consolidated financial statements (F-pages).\n\nThe Item 5 tables (T:A:384, T:A:385, T:A:455) are summaries in millions — derived from audited statements. Per instructions, don't use summary tables. Good — I'll use the primary statements.\n\nNow let me also verify the sign for Equity: The value is \"(592,216)\" which is negative. The XBRL tag has sgn=-. So value should be \"-592216\". As a signed decimal string without separators: \"-592216\".\n\nFor NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities: 913,081 positive, \"913081\".\n\nNow, for locations. The schema location object requires: accession, document, document_sha256, table, row, column, and html_anchor or page (one of them required via allOf/anyOf). Actually looking at the schema:\n\n```\n\"location\": {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\"properties\": {\"html_anchor\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"html_anchor\"]},\n        {\"properties\": {\"page\": {\"minimum\": 1, \"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"page\"]}\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"accession\": ...,\n    \"column\": ...,\n    \"document\": ...,\n    \"document_sha256\": ...,\n    \"html_anchor\": ...,\n    \"page\": ...,\n    \"row\": ...,\n    \"table\": ...\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"accession\", \"document\", \"document_sha256\", \"table\", \"row\", \"column\"]\n}\n```\n\nSo location requires accession, document, document_sha256, table, row, column, AND either html_anchor or page. Since this is an HTML document (d101275d20f.htm), I can use html_anchor. The anchors in the document appear as element identifiers like \"ixv-64800\" for the fact anchors. Hmm, the `<S:A:A:ixv-XXXXX;n=...>` elements — these look like inline XBRL anchors. The html_anchor could be \"ixv-64800\" etc. But do I know that's the actual HTML anchor? The document is an inline XBRL document, and \"ixv\" likely stands for \"inline XBRL value\". These seem like the anchor IDs.\n\nAlternatively, I could use page numbers. But the document doesn't have explicit page markers in the view... Actually, the source view doesn't include page numbers directly. The F-pages mention \"F-6\" etc. in the index. The consolidated statements of financial position is at F-6. But that's the index page reference. Hmm.\n\nActually, wait. This is a hybrid view of the HTML with structured anchors. The safest approach: use html_anchor with the ixv anchor IDs from the value cells. For example:\n- Total current assets: ixv-64800 (S:A:C638.12.8 contains S:A:A:ixv-64800;n=ifrs-full:CurrentAssets;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025)\n- Total assets: ixv-64823\n- Total current liabilities: ixv-64847\n- Total liabilities: ixv-64868\n- Total equity (deficit): ixv-64898\n- Total equity (deficit) and liabilities: ixv-64901\n- Net cash from operating activities: ixv-65207\n\nThese are the exact value cell anchors. The instruction says: \"Use the exact value cell's HTML anchor or the exact PDF page, table, row, and column.\"\n\nSo I'll use html_anchor = \"ixv-64800\" etc. And also provide table, row, column. What are the table, row, column identifiers? The table IDs in the view are like \"T:A:638\" for the assets table, \"T:A:639\" for liabilities/equity table, \"T:A:645\" for cash flows. Row could be the row label or the S:A:C###.##.1 row identifier. Column could be \"2025\" (the 2025 column).\n\nLet me define:\n- table: \"T:A:638\" (Consolidated statements of financial position — Assets section)\n- row: \"Total current assets\" (or the row element S:A:C638.12.1)\n- column: \"2025\"\n\nHmm, the schema requires table, row, column as minLength 1 strings. I'll use descriptive values: table: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (T:A:638)\", row: \"Total current assets\", column: \"2025\". Actually, I should probably keep them simple and verifiable. Let me use the S element IDs where possible.\n\nFor row, I could use \"S:A:C638.12.1\" but the row label \"Total current assets\" is clearer. I'll include both maybe: row: \"S:A:C638.12.1 (Total current assets)\". Hmm, that might be over-engineering. Let me just use the label.\n\nColumn: \"2025\" — the column header is \"2025\" (S:A:C638.2.6).\n\nNow, evidence_quote: \"maxLength\": 400, min 1. Should quote the text containing the value with statement context. For example: \"Total current assets ... 1,979,596\" — I'll quote something like \"Consolidated statements of financial position ... Total current assets ... 1,979,596\". The quote should contain the statement context and value. Let me construct quotes like:\n\n\"Total current assets  | $ 1,979,596\" — hmm, the actual cell text is \"1,979,596\" with a \"$\" preceding in some cells. For total current assets, the cell S:A:C638.12.8 contains just \"1,979,596\" (no $ in that cell; the $ is in C638.12.7? Actually looking at the markup: `<S:A:C638.12.8><S:A:A:ixv-64800;n=ifrs-full:CurrentAssets;...>1,979,596` — no \"$\" symbol immediately. For Total assets: `<S:A:C638.24.7>$ <S:A:C638.24.8>7,193,091`. For Total equity (deficit): `( 592,216 )` with sgn=-. For Total equity and liabilities: `$ 7,193,091`. For Net cash from operating activities: `913,081` (no $; the $ is on Income for the year row above).\n\nEvidence quotes I'll construct (paraphrasing the row context is fine, but the instruction says \"the quoted text contains its statement context and value\"). I'll include e.g.:\n\n- AssetsCurrent: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (As of December 31, 2025, in thousands of US dollars): Total current assets 1,979,596\"\n- Assets: \"Consolidated statements of financial position: Total assets $ 7,193,091 (2025, thousands of US dollars)\"\n- LiabilitiesCurrent: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (continued): Total current liabilities 3,095,938 (2025)\"\n- Liabilities: \"Total liabilities 7,785,307 (2025)\"\n- Equity: \"Total equity (deficit) (592,216) (2025)\"\n- EquityAndLiabilities: \"Total equity (deficit) and liabilities $ 7,193,091 (2025)\"\n- NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities: \"Consolidated statements of cash flows: Net cash from operating activities 913,081 (2025, in thousands of US dollars)\"\n\nHmm, but these quotes are reconstructions. In this document view, the actual rendered text includes pipes as separators. Let me make quotes that closely mirror the source content:\n\n- AssetsCurrent: \"Total current assets | $ 1,979,596\" — hmm, actually in the row S:A:C638.12.1: \"Total current assets |  |  |  |  | 1,979,596 |  | ...\" — the cell shows \"1,979,596\". Let me write: \"Total current assets 1,979,596\" plus mention \"(in thousands of US dollars)\".\n\nActually, I want the evidence quote to be faithful. Let me quote: \"Total current assets  |  1,979,596\" and note the statement header \"(In thousands of US dollars)\" separately in the quote. I think a quote like: \"Consolidated statements of financial position — As of December 31, 2025 — (In thousands of US dollars) — Total current assets: 1,979,596\" is acceptable as a compact representation containing context and value.\n\nLet me also double check the accounting basis: IFRS. The statements are prepared under IFRS Accounting Standards as issued by IASB (stated multiple times: \"have been prepared in accordance with International Financial Reporting Standards (\"IFRS\") Accounting Standards, as issued by the International Accounting Standards Board\"). So accounting_basis: \"IFRS\".\n\nConsolidation scope: consolidated. These are the \"Consolidated statements of financial position\" of Grupo Aeroméxico, S.A.B. de C.V. and subsidiaries. So \"consolidated\".\n\nCurrency: USD. Unit: USD. Scale: 1000 (thousands).\n\nPeriod: instant, end 2025-12-31, start null.\n\nFor cash flow: duration, start 2025-01-01, end 2025-12-31.\n\nNow, one consideration: Should the Equity field be negative? The row is \"Total equity (deficit)\" = (592,216), i.e., -592,216 thousand. The value cell has sgn=-. So value = \"-592216\". Yes.\n\nAlso, check for EquityAndLiabilities: 7,193,091 — matches Total assets, consistent.\n\nLet me also double-check whether there could be ambiguity with the Item 5 summary tables (in millions). The instruction says not to use summary tables when the definition requires consolidated primary-statement values. So the primary statements are the right source. There's no ambiguity between the two because I'm required to use the primary statement. For found results, only one location is cited, that's fine.\n\nBut hold on — should I double check that the primary consolidated statements of financial position are indeed present in the document and not just the Item 5 summary? Yes: T:A:638 and T:A:639 appear after \"Consolidated statements of financial position\" heading (S:A:B3420: \"Consolidated statements of financial position\", S:A:B3422: \"As of December 31, 2025, 2024 and 2023\", S:A:B3424: \"(In thousands of US dollars)\"). And T:A:639 is \"(continued)\" for liabilities and equity. Great.\n\nNow let me nail down the exact anchor IDs:\n\n1. Total current assets 2025: ixv-64800 (in S:A:C638.12.8)\n2. Total assets 2025: ixv-64823 (in S:A:C638.24.8)\n3. Total current liabilities 2025: ixv-64847 (in S:A:C639.13.8)\n4. Total liabilities 2025: ixv-64868 (in S:A:C639.24.8)\n5. Total equity (deficit) 2025: ixv-64898 (in S:A:C639.39.8)\n6. Total equity (deficit) and liabilities 2025: ixv-64901 (in S:A:C639.41.8)\n7. Net cash from operating activities 2025: ixv-65207 (in S:A:C645.36.8)\n\nLet me verify each from the document:\n\nT:A:638: `<S:A:C638.12.8><S:A:A:ixv-64800;n=ifrs-full:CurrentAssets;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3>1,979,596` ✓\n\n`<S:A:C638.24.7>$ <S:A:C638.24.8><S:A:A:ixv-64823;n=ifrs-full:Assets;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3>7,193,091` ✓\n\nT:A:639: `<S:A:C639.13.8><S:A:A:ixv-64847;n=ifrs-full:CurrentLiabilities;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3>3,095,938` ✓\n\n`<S:A:C639.24.8><S:A:A:ixv-64868;n=ifrs-full:Liabilities;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3>7,785,307` ✓\n\n`<S:A:C639.39.8>( <S:A:A:ixv-64898;n=ifrs-full:Equity;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3;sgn=->592,216 )` — the cell is \"( 592,216 )\" with sgn=- ✓ → value \"-592216\"\n\n`<S:A:C639.41.8><S:A:A:ixv-64901;n=ifrs-full:EquityAndLiabilities;ctx=PAsOn12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3>7,193,091` ✓\n\nT:A:645: `<S:A:C645.36.8><S:A:A:ixv-65207;n=ifrs-full:CashFlowsFromUsedInOperatingActivities;ctx=P01_01_2025To12_31_2025;u=Unit_USD;s=3;d=-3>913,081` ✓\n\nNote: the cash flow statement row is \"Net cash from operating activities\" — that matches the definition \"Net cash provided by or used in operating activities explicitly reported on the consolidated primary cash-flow statement.\" Good.\n\nScale: The statements say \"(In thousands of US dollars)\". The XBRL s=3 confirms thousands. Scale = \"1000\".\n\nHmm, wait — let me reconsider whether \"scale\" should be \"3\" or \"1000\". The schema pattern ^[1-9][0-9]*$ accepts both. The phrase \"Record the statement's scale separately; do not multiply it\" — the statement's scale as printed is \"In thousands of US dollars\", i.e., the multiplier 1000. I'll go with \"1000\". This is the more common interpretation in extraction pipelines where value × scale = reported amount. Value \"1979596\" × 1000 = 1,979,596 thousand = actual. Yes, \"1000\".\n\nActually hmm, one more thought: some schemas define scale as the power-of-ten exponent. But without explicit guidance, the multiplier interpretation (1000) is the most natural reading of \"scale.\" I'll go with \"1000\".\n\nNow about checked locations for found results: The found schema only has \"location\" (single object), no checked_locations array. So I just provide the single location. That's fine.\n\nFor each location:\n- accession: \"0001193125-26-197494\"\n- document: \"d101275d20f.htm\"\n- document_sha256: \"b842756f7ce62b0ae1bd2cf14d6fc3373c61297c0a74934f020493332415326e\"\n- table: e.g., \"T:A:638\" — hmm, but is \"T:A:638\" a meaningful table identifier in the source document? In this view format, tables are marked as <T:A:NNN>. I think it's fine to use that. But maybe more descriptive: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (T:A:638)\". The table field is just minLength 1 string. I'll use descriptive identifiers combining the view table marker.\n\nLet me decide: table: \"T:A:638 — Consolidated statements of financial position (assets)\". Hmm, adding em-dash may complicate. Keep it simple: table: \"T:A:638\". row: \"Total current assets\". column: \"2025\". html_anchor: \"ixv-64800\".\n\nFor the liabilities table: table: \"T:A:639\", row: \"Total current liabilities\", column: \"2025\", html_anchor: \"ixv-64847\". Etc.\n\nFor cash flows: table: \"T:A:645\", row: \"Net cash from operating activities\", column: \"2025\", html_anchor: \"ixv-65207\".\n\nColumn: the column header in these tables is \"2025\" (S:A:C638.2.6, S:A:C639.2.6, S:A:C645.2.6). So column: \"2025\".\n\nShould I include page? The schema allows either html_anchor or page (anyOf requires one of them). I'll use html_anchor only. Note that \"html_anchor\" property also appears in properties with type [\"string\",\"null\"], but the allOf anyOf requires html_anchor with minLength 1 OR page integer ≥1. So providing html_anchor as a non-empty string satisfies it.\n\nEvidence quotes — let me craft them carefully to contain statement context and value:\n\n1. AssetsCurrent: \"Consolidated statements of financial position — As of December 31, 2025 — (In thousands of US dollars) — Total current assets: 1,979,596\"\n   Actually maybe better to mimic the row: \"Total current assets  |  $ 1,979,596\". Hmm, in the markup the $ appears for some rows. For the current assets row there's no $. Let me just quote: \"Total current assets 1,979,596\" and include header context: \"Consolidated statements of financial position, As of December 31, 2025, 2024 and 2023 (In thousands of US dollars): Total current assets 1,979,596\". That's within 400 chars. Good.\n\n2. Assets: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (In thousands of US dollars): Total assets $ 7,193,091 (2025 column)\"\n\n3. LiabilitiesCurrent: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (continued) (In thousands of US dollars): Total current liabilities 3,095,938 (2025 column)\"\n\n4. Liabilities: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (continued) (In thousands of US dollars): Total liabilities 7,785,307 (2025 column)\"\n\n5. Equity: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (continued) (In thousands of US dollars): Total equity (deficit) ( 592,216 ) (2025 column)\"\n\n6. EquityAndLiabilities: \"Consolidated statements of financial position (continued) (In thousands of US dollars): Total equity (deficit) and liabilities $ 7,193,091 (2025 column)\"\n\n7. NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities: \"Consolidated statements of cash flows (In thousands of US dollars): Net cash from operating activities 913,081 (2025 column)\"\n\nThese quotes include statement context and value. Good.\n\nSource labels:\n- AssetsCurrent: \"Total current assets\"\n- Assets: \"Total assets\"\n- LiabilitiesCurrent: \"Total current liabilities\"\n- Liabilities: \"Total liabilities\"\n- Equity: \"Total equity (deficit)\"\n- EquityAndLiabilities: \"Total equity (deficit) and liabilities\"\n- NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities: \"Net cash from operating activities\"\n\nValues (signed decimal strings without separators):\n- AssetsCurrent: \"1979596\"\n- Assets: \"7193091\"\n- LiabilitiesCurrent: \"3095938\"\n- Liabilities: \"7785307\"\n- Equity: \"-592216\"\n- EquityAndLiabilities: \"7193091\"\n- NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities: \"913081\"\n\nScale: \"1000\" for all.\n\nUnit: \"USD\" for all.\n\nCurrency: \"USD\" for all.\n\nAccounting basis: \"IFRS\" for all.\n\nConsolidation scope: \"consolidated\" for all.\n\nPeriod:\n- Balance sheet items: {\"kind\": \"instant\", \"start\": null, \"end\": \"2025-12-31\"}\n- Cash flow: {\"kind\": \"duration\", \"start\": \"2025-01-01\", \"end\": \"2025-12-31\"}\n\nRequested field names (copy exactly):\n- \"AssetsCurrent\", \"Assets\", \"LiabilitiesCurrent\", \"Liabilities\", \"Equity\", \"EquityAndLiabilities\", \"NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities\"\n\nTop-level output:\n{\"schema\": \"statement_candidate_v1\", \"request_id\": \"pilot-aero-primary-v1\", \"results\": [...]}\n\nLet me double-check the equity figure sign convention. In the balance sheet, \"Equity (deficit)\" section shows \"Total equity (deficit)\" of (592,216) for 2025 — negative equity (deficit). The instruction: \"Record the printed number as a signed decimal string without separators\" — the printed number is (592,216), which is negative. So \"-592216\". ✓\n\nOne more check: should I consider the possibility of ambiguity between the Item 5 summary table (millions: Total current assets 1,979.6) and the primary statement (thousands: 1,979,596)? These are consistent (1,979.6 million ≈ 1,979,596 thousand). No ambiguity — the primary statement governs per the field definition (\"on the consolidated primary balance sheet\"). So found is appropriate.\n\nAlso verify the cash flow: 913,081 thousand = $913.1 million, matches Item 5 summary \"Net cash from operating activities 913.1\". ✓ Consistent.\n\nAlso, should I worry that \"Consolidated statements of financial position\" includes 2025, 2024, 2023 columns and I'm targeting 2025? The 2025 column is the first data column (S:A:C638.2.6 header \"2025\"). ✓\n\nLet me also confirm the document sha256 matches: \"b842756f7ce62b0ae1bd2cf14d6fc3373c61297c0a74934f020493332415326e\" — from the manifest, yes, and the @@DOCUMENT line confirms raw_sha256=b842756f7ce62b0ae1bd2cf14d6fc3373c61297c0a74934f020493332415326e. ✓\n\nNow, regarding html_anchor format: the anchors in the document appear as \"ixv-64800\" (inline XBRL value element). I'll use that as the html_anchor string. Since this is a rendered view of an iXBRL document, these are plausibly the element IDs. Alternatively, I could use \"S:A:C638.12.8\" (the value cell element ID). The instruction says \"Use the exact value cell's HTML anchor\". The value cell is S:A:C638.12.8, and within it the anchored fact is ixv-64800. Hmm. Which is the \"HTML anchor\"? The ixv- elements have the pattern `<S:A:A:ixv-64800;n=...>` — these are anchor elements (\"A\" might stand for anchor). I'll use \"ixv-64800\" as the html_anchor since those are the fact anchors embedded in the value cells. Actually, to be safe and maximally informative, maybe use both: html_anchor: \"ixv-64800\". The cell ID is in the row/column context anyway via table/row/column fields.\n\nHmm, actually, let me reconsider: I could put html_anchor as \"ixv-64800\" and it directly anchors the value. That aligns with \"the exact value cell's HTML anchor\". The ixv anchors are the value elements. Good.\n\nNow let me also think about whether to include page. The financial statements are at pages F-6 etc. per the index, but the actual page numbers in the HTML/PDF aren't given in the view. I'll omit page and just use html_anchor.\n\nLet me now double check schema compliance for found objects:\n\nRequired: requested_field, outcome, value, scale, source_label, unit, currency, period, accounting_basis, consolidation_scope, location, evidence_quote.\n\n- requested_field: string ✓\n- outcome: \"found\" ✓\n- value: string matching ^-?(0|[1-9][0-9]*)(\\.[0-9]+)?$ — \"1979596\" ✓, \"7193091\" ✓, \"3095938\" ✓, \"7785307\" ✓, \"-592216\" ✓, \"913081\" ✓\n- scale: string matching ^[1-9][0-9]*$ — \"1000\" ✓\n- source_label: \"Total current assets\" etc. ✓\n- unit: \"USD\" matches ^(?:[A-Z]{3}|[A-Z]{3}/shares|shares|pure)$ ✓\n- currency: \"USD\" matches ^[A-Z]{3}$ ✓\n- period: {\"kind\": \"instant\", \"start\": null, \"end\": \"2025-12-31\"} — required kind, start, end. start can be null (type [\"string\",\"null\"]) ✓. For duration: {\"kind\":\"duration\",\"start\":\"2025-01-01\",\"end\":\"2025-12-31\"} ✓\n- accounting_basis: \"IFRS\" ✓\n- consolidation_scope: \"consolidated\" ✓\n- location: object with accession, document, document_sha256, table, row, column, html_anchor. additionalProperties false — so only these keys allo